{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And they believed.</b> After they heard that HaShem had visited them, for the end spoken to Abraham had arrived." "<b>Afflicted.</b> From the root עינוי (affliction)." "<b>And they bowed.</b> Of the doubled-root class, like קדקד, on the pattern of 'ויתמו ימי בכי אבל משה' (Deuteronomy 34:8); ידמו כאבן (below, 9:16). And those who say they are of the nun-class — would that ידמו כאבן were like them, for they multiply roots that are not in the holy language on account of the pattern. Do they not see that 'רדו' (Genesis 42:2) is on the pattern of 'בנו לכם בתים' (Jeremiah 29:5), and they are roots? For whatever we can avoid making into multiple roots on account of the pattern, that is correct."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:47.430916903Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}